\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Hosanna, loud hosanna,
\par The little children sang;
\par Through pillared court and temple,
\par The lovely anthem rang;
\par To Jesus, who has blessed them,
\par Close folded to His breast,
\par The children sang their praises,
\par The simplest and the best.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. From Olivet they followed,
\par Midst an exultant crowd,
\par Waving the victor palm branch,
\par And shouting clear and loud.
\par Bright angels joined the chorus,
\par Beyond the cloudless sky:
\par Hosanna in the highest,
\par Glory to God on high!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Fair leaves of silvery olive
\par They strewed upon the ground,
\par Whilst Salem's circling mountains
\par Echoed the joyful sound.
\par The Lord of men and angels
\par Rode on in high lowly state,
\par Nor scorned that little children
\par Should on His bidding wait.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Hosanna in the highest!
\par That ancient song we sing;
\par For Christ is our Redeemer,
\par The Lord of heaven our King:
\par O may we ever praise Him,
\par With heart and life and voice,
\par And in His blissful presence
\par Eternally rejoice.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

